<% content_for :title, "Support · Knowledge Vault" %>
<div class="kv-page">
  <div class="kv-page-header">
    <div class="kv-heading-group">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p>Get help with Knowledge Vault and the Slack bot.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-static-content">
    <section class="kv-static-section">
      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <p>New to Knowledge Vault? Start at our <%= link_to "Installation", installation_path %> page to create an account and connect Slack. After that, upload documents from the Documents page and ask questions from the Q&A page or by mentioning the bot in Slack.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="kv-static-section">
      <h2>Slack bot</h2>
      <p>Mention the bot in a channel or DM to ask questions. The bot uses the documents in your organization’s knowledge base to answer. Only workspaces connected via Integrations in the app can use the bot. If the bot doesn’t respond, check that Slack is connected under Integrations and that you’ve uploaded documents.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="kv-static-section">
      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>For technical issues, feature requests, or general questions, reach out via your preferred channel (e.g. the contact method you use for your organization). If you don’t have a contact yet, use the email or support channel associated with your Knowledge Vault deployment.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-soft-divider"></div>
  <p class="kv-meta-text kv-meta-muted">
    <%= link_to "Install app", installation_path %> · <%= link_to "Privacy policy", privacy_path %>
  </p>
</div>
